The handoff regression is reproducibly flaky, and the stack dump shows why: concurrent callers spend over six seconds rescanning every macOS path component in `_prepare_for_acquire`, before the configured five-second lock timeout even starts. That is a real task-scoped concurrency failure. I’m completing build/provenance checks, then I’ll persist a `changes_requested` verdict with this exact reproduction and route it to `to-dev`.
